RELGEN(1)                     ZOAU Command Syntax                     RELGEN(1)

DISCLAIMER
	Internal ZOAU utility, behavior may change without prior notice.

NAME

	relgen - Relative generation resolution.

SYNOPSIS

	relgen [-dhv] GENERATION_RELATIVE_NAME

	-d
		Print out debug messages.

	-h
		Display syntax help.

	-v
		Print verbose information.


DESCRIPTION

	relgen resolves a relative generation number into an absolute generation
	name.

EXAMPLES

	Resolve the latest generation from the generation data group 'ZOAUSER.GDG'

		relgen 'ZOAUSER.GDG(0)'

EXIT VALUES

	0
		Successful resolution of the relative generation name.

	other
		Error resolving the relative name. See error messages for details.

SEE ALSO

	dls(1)
